   "contentMd": "# Facebook web login checkpoint loop — 2026-09-20/21\n\n**Symptom:** Facebook web login failed on every desktop Chrome (tony-omen + tony-dell, normal AND incognito). Each attempt redirected to `facebook.com/two_step_verification/authentication/?flow=pre_authentication` plus an Arkose/reCAPTCHA iframe on `fbsbx.com`, then bounced back to the logged-out homepage — no `c_user`/`xs` session cookies were ever issued. Mobile app stayed logged in the whole time. Nothing appeared in the app's login alerts or \"Where you're logged in\" (pre-auth checkpoints never reach the session stage).\n\n**Root cause:** Facebook's server-side risk engine flagged web logins for the account — NOT a Chrome, cookie, extension, DNS, or IP problem. Verified: clean-profile Chrome loaded the login page fine; cookies/clear-on-exit settings normal; UA-switcher extension disabled; residential True Online IP unremarkable.\n\n**Resolution:** Cleared on its own ~24h later (Facebook-side flag expired / changed). Confirmed working 2026-09-21.\n\n**Playbook for next time:**\n- Stop retrying — every failed captcha attempt deepens the flag.\n- On the logged-in mobile app: Settings → Accounts Centre → Password and security → Two-factor authentication → check the configured method, generate recovery codes; check the in-app notification bell for \"approve this login\".\n- Tether desktop to phone hotspot once — if cellular IP logs straight in, the home IP was flagged.\n- `m.facebook.com` / `mbasic.facebook.com` sometimes pass under lighter checkpoint thresholds.\n- Last resort: `facebook.com/recover` password reset — resets checkpoint state, but only attempt once.\n- Diagnostic shortcut that worked here: Chrome History SQLite (`Default/History`) shows the `two_step_verification` + `fbsbx.com/captcha` redirect chain; cookie jar missing `c_user`/`xs` proves the session never established.",
   "addedAt": 1789995846,
   "updatedAt": 1790001244
  },
